  "natural_statement": "For every natural r and finite indexed family t_e of distinct nonzero Boolean points with |E|>3r, put R=F2[T_ij] (three rows), F=Frac(R), z_i(e)=sum_j T_ij^2 t_ej, M_e,(i,j)=t_ej z_i(e), and c(e)=(sum_j T_0j t_ej)(sum_j T_1j t_ej)(sum_j T_2j t_ej). Then c(e)^2=z_0(e)z_1(e)z_2(e), and c is outside the F-column span of the actual matrix M. Moreover there exists P in R with P nonzero and totalDegree(P)<=6r+3 such that, for every commutative characteristic-two ring S and every assignment T* in S^(3r), if there are weights a_ij in S with sum_ij a_ij M_e,(i,j)(T*)=c(e)(T*) for every e, then P(T*)=0. The same obstruction holds for arbitrary ring homomorphisms R to S. In characteristic-two fields the specialized c(e) is the unique square root of the specialized product of the z_i(e). No distribution, probability bound, or geometric-extension-to-linear-system reduction is asserted as compiler-verified here.",
